posts.body:
Frequently playing Counter Strike Global Offensive. Nothing but rush B, plant the bomb, camping and snipe, clutch, defuse the bomb.......Terrorist Wins(always says by game announcer). Yup, you know the game........until a month, I didn’t play it and my performance gone bad when I played it back.
Now, I’m playing Gaia’s Melody : Echoed Melodies because I saw Echo607 posted her latest LP videos on Youtube. So, I gonna beat the game before she’ll post last episode of her LP game.
@Philosophus Vagus
How ‘bout Crash?
@TheoAllen
No wonder you asked for help.

I enjoy the "start with nothing and start building" base type games too. I've been playing a lot of The Forest the past couple of weeks. It's survival horror, with a sort of loose story as you discover things about the island. It leaves early access at the end of this month and is pretty polished by this stage, so I'm looking forward to the big update on the 30th.
@ValkyrieDesign
How are you finding BotW? I really enjoyed it, I was playing for weeks, shield-surfing around the place and getting owned by lynels

@Spoofuss
...liked better than what?
And for what reasons do you like it better than whatever else?

@Engr. Adiktuzmiko
Sure it does work well in handheld. I played through the first temple like that but then I got the chance to plug it into a 55” TV and play with a PRO controller... and that experience was so much better. Mostly because the control in handheld can’t stack up to the comfort of the PRO controller but there’s other things too. Battery time for example, and the fact that the switch is kinda heavy so holding it in front of you for more than 1 hour isn’t that comfortable. And Zeldas grand landscapes look marvelous on a large screen.
I’m in no rush. Soon I’ll probably be playing Pokémon Let’s go Picachuu anyway...

@Mr. Detective
I don’t remember saving Kanji being that hard? Unless you’re trying to clear the entire dungeon in one try/day? I didn’t grind much and focused on the social parts of the game but since you’ll be warned ahead of time you can easily afford 3-5 drives or more into each dungeon without sacrificing much of the more interesting story and social events.
To be honest, I’ve not finished P4:Golden (yet), but it’s more because the game is so frikking long that it feels like it’ll never end. I think I’m like 80~90 hours into the game and it’s not done yet...

@MechScapeZH
Oh what's the post game like in Arcadia?
I'm a pretty big fan but mainly stick to the older stuff. Synchros are kind of fun but my main jam was oldschool yugioh. Favourite yugioh game? Probably... Ultimate Masters 2006(my games actually inspired by it). I like how they just say screw it, you don't care about the story. Here's a bunch of monsters you can duel. Have fun!

@MechScapeZH
Card games and RPG's are my favourite.
Boss Rush eh? Hmm... Think I should check it out once I knock out a few of my other yugioh games. Don't think I'll ever stop playing the yugioh games.

@MechScapeZH
I'm only on the first world at the moment so I've only seen the first 4 monsters. Penguin Knight, Skull Servant a plant type and one other. I found the dialogue from the monsters a bit jarring. Penguin Knight calling me beautiful got me going "hey now... Is a yugioh card trying to flirt with me?"
Oh Mega Man? Cool! Only Mega Man I played was 9 for the ps3 and then only a level or two so I don't know much about the series but I like how difficult Megaman 9 was.

@MechScapeZH
Oh, pool of water? Ok thanks I'll check for when it's animated and thanks, will try to star all the Structure decks.
Since you put hundreds of hours in this game there must be a ton of content. I'm getting a lot more XP than I did on Troubadour too which is great. Should be able to make multiple decks in that case(Troubadour only gave 100 per duel and this gets you (at least now) 500 per duel).
